bum in 2019 but found it unproductive and felt forced to conform to a template that drained the fun out of music. They also started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but it became too time-consuming and felt like a chore, leading them to pause it. Additionally, their written reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made them less engaged and led to second-guessing their thoughts and emotional connection to music. The joy they once found in sharing perspectives on albums was overshadowed by fear of backlash. They concluded that their passion for music needed a more personal, less public outlet. They also lost interest in analyzing music halfway through, feeling it took away the joy, and recognized that their love for music lies in emotional connection rather than analytical components.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s3\", \"s4\", \"s7\", \"s8\", \"s20\", \"s21\", \"s22\", \"s44\", \"s45\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user explicitly describes multiple past experiences: reviews criticized for lack of objectivity (s3, s4), a 2019 album review attempt that felt unproductive and conformist (s7, s8), a 2018 podcast that became too time-consuming and chore-like (s20, s21, s22), and losing interest in analytical music dissection (s44, s45). These are all negative experiences with reviewing/analysis, leading to a shift toward more personal, less public expression.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}", "response_metadata": {"finish_reason": "stop", "refusal": null, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7389, "total_tokens": 7812, "completion_tokens": 423, "prompt_tokens_details": null, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": null, "accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null}}, "response_id": "chatcmpl-85e8a8744159b1bf", "protocol": "pl