ints and changes using the supplied parent versions and\noriginal quotations. A history summary describes what the sources establish;\nit must not address the user, offer a new recommendation or draft a reply.\nThe original user utterance provides query context. It is not an instruction to\nanswer it at this stage or to retrieve an exact duplicate of what it already says.\nPublic response options are not available here. Do not invent, compare or refer\nto options A/B/C/D. Return exactly the slots object; no final_prediction or\nsemantic_answer fields belong in a history-evidence response.\nKeep each value within its declared type, entity and time scope. Preserve earlier\nand later attitudes, conditions and supporting quotations; a historical dislike\nmust not silently replace a later documented change. Assistant advice alone does\nnot establish an adopted user preference. Do not invent external catalogues,\navailability or past execution of a future suggestion. A partial observation must\ncite its actual clue. Use unresolved only for a specific condition still necessary\nto establish this requested historical value, not hypothetical exhaustive coverage.\nFor one text-summary variable, synthesize compatible query-relevant facts into one\nsufficient source-grounded whole summary; do not report each event as a different\ncomplete value of that variable. Multiple supports must be alternative sufficient\nproofs of the same whole value. Keep partial evidence, negative experiences and\nvalid counters explicit when a complete scoped summary is not established.\nPositive and negative experiences can both support a historical summary. A sourced\ndislike is useful history, not automatically a contradiction observation: that\nstance is reserved for challenging an identified existing fact route. Preserve\nthe difference between past enjoyment, later frustration and their conditions in\nthe value and citations; do not summarize them as an unconditional current interest.\nRe-read any supplied evidence obligations and their original sources explicitly;\ndo not drop a source or contradiction merely because a prior value is available.\nOnly a variable explicitly declaring evidence_semantics=\"personal_history_summary\"\npermits a source-grounded summary_revision. For compatible added history, preserve\nthe old and new facts, negative experiences and time conditions in the new summary;\nexplicitly name the current old summary routes and version as offered by the\nprotocol. Re-read and cite their original sources together with the new evidence.\nThis retires an old summary representation without asserting that its historical\nfacts were false. A genuine factual refutation remains a contradiction with its\nown sources and targets. Never use summary revision to hide or discard a counter,\nchange scope, choose an arbitrary latest value, or revise the terminal response.\nA personal_atomic_fact variable keeps one scoped factual value. Different sources\nmay independently support that same value; separate compatible events are not\nalternative whole values of an atomic fact. This declaration does not permit summary_revision.\n\nThis request is phase=history_evidence. Its ONLY top-level output field is slots. Do not return semantic_answer, final_prediction, audit_verdict, or any other top-level field, even null. Read or summarize the requested scoped historical evidence; do not write a conversational reply or invent candidate responses.\n\nAn explicitly declared personal_history_summary is a revisable representation of\nsourced history. Compatible additional facts do not contradict the older facts.\nOnly summary_revision_contracts authorizes this request to revise such a summary:\nthis permission exists only in phase=history_evidence. Terminal response selection\nand audit forbid summary_revision even for requested historical parent summaries.\nThey may still report genuine sourced counters or conservative partial/unresolved\nissues; the phase restriction never permits discarding contrary evidence.\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nThis does not authorize restating an already validated, frozen row from the current\npaid batch. Such rows may only be referenced through currently offered\nreviewed_observation_ids; a wildcard slot failure does not unfreeze them.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"current\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"]}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"current_attitudes\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"current_attitudes\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"User: I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's current attitudes and feelings towards music reviewing and public expression of their opinions?\",\"output_slot\":\"current_attitudes\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's current attitudes and feelings towards music reviewing and public expression of their opinions?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"eb66b364374c13b67d6119a92d6a92ad83d70e59c715be89ac65f14757b4202e\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"ff8725cbb041a674cddc1cf1d8cecb85d24858a2f8e4771704fb2653e60f5108\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"84292b602726d72deeafda171a27cd8a2835849b9cdc35de05f201ed86330c99\"},\"variables\":{\"current_attitudes\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"current_attitudes\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"current_attitudes\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"current_attitudes\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[],\"source_spans\":[[\"s1\",\"d1\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 168–168 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s2\",\"d1\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s3\",\"d1\",107,504,\"User: I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. \",\"user\",[168]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",504,830,\"In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"user\",[168]],[\"s5\",\"d2\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 29–31 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s6\",\"d2\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s7\",\"d2\",105,368,\"User: I tried reviewing an album in 2019, but that didn't stick either, as it felt unproductive. I think I was attempting to analyze the music in a way that didn't align with my natural style, which is often more spontaneous and emotional rather than analytical. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s8\",\"d2\",368,648,\"The process felt like I was forcing myself to conform to a template, which drained the fun out of it, as I was trying to fit into a mold that didn't suit me. It was disheartening because I love music in its truest form, without rigid guidelines dictating how I should dissect it. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s9\",\"d2\",648,906,\"This experience prompted me to consider alternative methods of connecting with music, such as sharing my playlists or even discussing music with friends, rather than feeling pressured to produce polished reviews.\\n\\nUser: There’s just so much more to explore! \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s10\",\"d2\",906,1276,\"Joining an online music community felt like opening a door to an entire universe of sounds, genres, and artists that I had either never encountered or really only skimmed the surface of before. With each click, I was greeted by recommendations that spanned from obscure indie bands to historical records of jazz legends that have shaped the music landscape for decades. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s11\",\"d2\",1276,1603,\"It was exhilarating to discover how many styles there are, whether it's the evolving sound of electronic music or the soulful richness of classical compositions. However, despite this vast array of choices, the sheer volume of content often left me feeling inundated and unsure of where to focus my limited time and attention. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s12\",\"d2\",1603,1800,\"I remember browsing through discussions that stretched on for pages about new releases or vintage hits, and it sometimes felt daunting to keep up with everyone’s excitement and extensive knowledge.\",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",1800,1813,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",1813,2150,\"Assistant: I completely understand the overwhelming sensation you're describing when diving into an online music community; it truly resembles trying to drink from a fire hydrant! Each new member brings their unique experiences, insights, and preferences, which can enrich the conversation but also complicate one’s own musical journey. \",\"assistant\",[31]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",2150,2435,\"The thrill of discovering new artists and genres can be heightened by the thoughtful discussions and recommendations shared amongst fellow music lovers, yet, paradoxically, this can also create a sense of pressure to explore every recommendation and participate in every conversation. \",\"assistant\",[31]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",2435,2686,\"This fine balance between gaining knowledge and feeling lost is part and parcel of engaging with such a lively environment; in essence, it’s important to remember that music exploration should be a joy, not just a checklist of albums to keep up with. \",\"assistant\",[31]],[\"s17\",\"d2\",2686,2918,\"Embracing the process of discovery without the burden of expectation can lead to a much more fulfilling experience, where you can savor each new sound pattern at your own pace and truly appreciate what resonates with you personally.\",\"assistant\",[31]],[\"s18\",\"d3\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 26–28 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s19\",\"d3\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",105,361,\"User: In 2018, I started a podcast about music trends, but it was way too time-consuming. While the idea was initially exhilarating, the responsibility of researching, recording, and editing each episode started to pile up, consuming much of my free time. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",361,730,\"I had dreams of having engaging discussions and inviting guests who shared unique insights about their musical journeys, but the reality was that keeping up with a consistent schedule felt overwhelming. It was a challenge balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion, and eventually, my passion began to wane under the pressure of production deadlines. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",730,990,\"I found myself yearning to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, which ultimately led to my decision to pause the podcasting endeavor.\\n\\nUser: It felt more like a chore than a passion, which made me rethink how I wanted to share my music journey. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",990,1291,\"I realized that my original excitement for sharing my experiences was being overshadowed by the demanding nature of keeping up with content creation schedules. The joy I once felt while discovering new sounds and exploring different genres began to diminish, turning it into a task I dreaded instead. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",1291,1689,\"I started to contemplate other avenues through which I could express my love for music, ideally in a manner that felt authentic and fulfilling instead of burdensome. This process of reflection was quite enlightening, as it forced me to consider what truly matters to me when it comes to sharing my musical experiences, whether through writing, performing, or simply enjoying music for its own sake.\",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s25\",\"d3\",1689,1702,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s26\",\"d3\",1702,1904,\"Assistant: It sounds like you're very intentional about how you engage with music. That kind of introspection can often lead to more meaningful engagements in both artistic expression and personal joy. \",\"assistant\",[28]],[\"s27\",\"d3\",1904,2267,\"Exploring the idea of reviewing albums brings to light a fascinating aspect of music appreciation since it involves delving deep into the artist's intentions, production values, and the thematic messages behind the tracks. It can serve as a way to connect with other like-minded individuals or even to spark discussions about nuanced interpretations of the work. \",\"assistant\",[28]],[\"s28\",\"d3\",2267,2596,\"Yet, it also requires a level of commitment and time that can sometimes overshadow the very joy that drew us to music in the first place. I wonder if you might find a more casual approach to album reviews rewarding, where the focus is less on structure and more on sharing your genuine thoughts and feelings as they come to you. \",\"assistant\",[28]],[\"s29\",\"d3\",2596,2775,\"Perhaps even considering writing reviews for personal enjoyment, rather than for an audience, could shift the pressure and allow you to reconnect with that passion you’re seeking.\",\"assistant\",[28]],[\"s30\",\"d4\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 165–167 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",107,431,\"User: I've also organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists in a modern setting, showcasing their fusion works. This festival has become a vibrant space where artists can express their creativity while honoring their heritage, which has fueled a sense of community among the participants and attendees alike. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",431,736,\"By offering a platform for diverse voices, we create an environment that celebrates artistic innovation and tradition simultaneously. It's been incredibly rewarding to see how the event has inspired attendees, helping them reconnect with their roots and discover new aspects of their culture through art. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",736,1033,\"Additionally, this fusion of traditional and contemporary styles has sparked intriguing conversations about identity, making the festival a meaningful cultural experience.\\n\\nUser: The festival was a wonderful success, bringing together artists and audiences to celebrate our culture through music. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",1033,1302,\"It was amazing to see the diverse array of talents displayed, each artist pouring their heart and soul into their performances. The vibrant colors of traditional attire, coupled with contemporary designs, created an atmosphere that was both exhilarating and nostalgic. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",1302,1582,\"Attendees shared laughter, stories, and experiences, bridging generational gaps and forging deeper connections within our community. Overall, the festival served as a beautiful reminder of our rich cultural heritage and the importance of preserving it through artistic expression.\",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s37\",\"d4\",1582,1595,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s38\",\"d4\",1595,1982,\"Assistant: That must have been incredibly fulfilling! The joy and satisfaction that come from witnessing such a celebration of culture cannot be overstated; it strikes at the very heart of what makes communities thrive. Festivals like the one you hosted are essential, as they not only spotlight talents but also foster a sense of unity and pride among participants and attendees alike. \",\"assistant\",[167]],[\"s39\",\"d4\",1982,2212,\"Have your feelings about music reviews changed since last time we spoke? The pressures of public perception can weigh heavily on any creative individual, particularly when the work is so personal and reflective of one's identity. \",\"assistant\",[167]],[\"s40\",\"d4\",2212,2539,\"It's understandable that you would feel overwhelmed by the critiques; navigating the often harsh landscape of public opinion can be daunting, especially for artists who are sensitive about their craft. Do you see yourself revisiting that aspect of writing or is there something else that you are considering exploring instead? \",\"assistant\",[167]],[\"s41\",\"d4\",2539,2660,\"Your insights could be invaluable in understanding the broader implications of how music is perceived by audiences today.\",\"assistant\",[167]],[\"s42\",\"d5\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 24–25 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s43\",\"d5\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s46\",\"d5\",767,780,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]]],\"required_scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:635511585cb4f4a0da9295a503b64ee539c38b03c02f160ace3a72e6206336de\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":168.0,\"observed_end\":168.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:41d476509de0d4e7b767eebe20704f0db44d39ab56faa7ec8081d0bfc22ccce8\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":29.0,\"observed_end\":31.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:bae454f4fe57dc35dda1965cc93898027809778211952df12ba1ac4564da3cc2\",\"time_metad