ticism, pressure, and loss of joy, and are now embracing more personal, less public forms of musical expression and community engagement, such as organizing a festival.\",\"variable\":\"current_attitudes\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},{\"id\":\"fact_6a88725b5da0855a58b876cc\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly states that external criticism made them less engaged and that they now prefer a more personal, less public way to express their passion (s3, s4). They tried reviewing albums in 2019 but found it unproductive and misaligned with their spontaneous, emotional style (s7, s8). They prefer alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing music with friends (s9). They started a podcast in 2018 but found it too time-consuming and burdensome, leading them to pause it (s20, s21, s22, s23, s24). They lost interest in music theory analysis because it took away joy (s44, s45). They organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists, finding it rewarding and community-building (s32, s33, s34, s35, s36). These sources collectively support the user's current preferences for emotional, informal, and community-oriented music engagement.\",\"variable\":\"music_preferences\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t2\"},{\"id\":\"fact_0578095f03f34ed22c798ec3\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user describes multiple phases: early analytical reviews criticized (s3), joy overshadowed by fear of backlash (s4), failed attempts at structured reviews in 2019 (s7, s8), considering alternative methods like sharing playlists (s9), starting a podcast in 2018 that became overwhelming (s20, s21, s22, s23, s24), losing interest in technical analysis (s44, s45), and later successfully organizing a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists (s32, s33, s34, s35, s36). The overall trajectory shows a shift from public, analytical, structured expression to more personal, community-oriented, and less public forms.\",\"variable\":\"changes_in_expression\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t3\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",107,504,\"User: I found that my reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made me less engaged in the process. It felt like I was constantly under the microscope, where every word I wrote was scrutinized by people who often missed the nuance of my opinion. This external pressure led me to second-guess not only my thoughts but also my emotional connection to the music I was discussing. \",\"user\",[168]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",504,830,\"In the end, I realized that the joy I once found in sharing my perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash, and that’s a heavy burden for anyone. It became clearer to me that my passion for music needed to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, which is something I’m finally starting to embrace.\",\"user\",[168]],[\"s7\",\"d2\",105,368,\"User: I tried reviewing an album in 2019, but that didn't stick either, as it felt unproductive. I think I was attempting to analyze the music in a way that didn't align with my natural style, which is often more spontaneous and emotional rather than analytical. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s8\",\"d2\",368,648,\"The process felt like I was forcing myself to conform to a template, which drained the fun out of it, as I was trying to fit into a mold that didn't suit me. It was disheartening because I love music in its truest form, without rigid guidelines dictating how I should dissect it. \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s9\",\"d2\",648,906,\"This experience prompted me to consider alternative methods of connecting with music, such as sharing my playlists or even discussing music with friends, rather than feeling pressured to produce polished reviews.\\n\\nUser: There’s just so much more to explore! \",\"user\",[29,30]],[\"s20\",\"d3\",105,361,\"User: In 2018, I started a podcast about music trends, but it was way too time-consuming. While the idea was initially exhilarating, the responsibility of researching, recording, and editing each episode started to pile up, consuming much of my free time. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",361,730,\"I had dreams of having engaging discussions and inviting guests who shared unique insights about their musical journeys, but the reality was that keeping up with a consistent schedule felt overwhelming. It was a challenge balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion, and eventually, my passion began to wane under the pressure of production deadlines. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s22\",\"d3\",730,990,\"I found myself yearning to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, which ultimately led to my decision to pause the podcasting endeavor.\\n\\nUser: It felt more like a chore than a passion, which made me rethink how I wanted to share my music journey. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",990,1291,\"I realized that my original excitement for sharing my experiences was being overshadowed by the demanding nature of keeping up with content creation schedules. The joy I once felt while discovering new sounds and exploring different genres began to diminish, turning it into a task I dreaded instead. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",1291,1689,\"I started to contemplate other avenues through which I could express my love for music, ideally in a manner that felt authentic and fulfilling instead of burdensome. This process of reflection was quite enlightening, as it forced me to consider what truly matters to me when it comes to sharing my musical experiences, whether through writing, performing, or simply enjoying music for its own sake.\",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",107,431,\"User: I've also organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists in a modern setting, showcasing their fusion works. This festival has become a vibrant space where artists can express their creativity while honoring their heritage, which has fueled a sense of community among the participants and attendees alike. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",431,736,\"By offering a platform for diverse voices, we create an environment that celebrates artistic innovation and tradition simultaneously. It's been incredibly rewarding to see how the event has inspired attendees, helping them reconnect with their roots and discover new aspects of their culture through art. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",736,1033,\"Additionally, this fusion of traditional and contemporary styles has sparked intriguing conversations about identity, making the festival a meaningful cultural experience.\\n\\nUser: The festival was a wonderful success, bringing together artists and audiences to celebrate our culture through music. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",1033,1302,\"It was amazing to see the diverse array of talents displayed, each artist pouring their heart and soul into their performances. The vibrant colors of traditional attire, coupled with contemporary designs, created an atmosphere that was both exhilarating and nostalgic. \",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",1302,1582,\"Attendees shared laughter, stories, and experiences, bridging generational gaps and forging deeper connections within our community. Overall, the festival served as a beautiful reminder of our rich cultural heritage and the importance of preserving it through artistic expression.\",\"user\",[165,166]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]]],\"required_parent_versions\":{\"reviewing_experiences\":{},\"current_attitudes\":{},\"music_preferences\":{},\"changes_in_expression\":{},\"user_context_summary\":{\"reviewing_experiences\":1,\"current_attitudes\":1,\"music_preferences\":1,\"changes_in_expression\":1}},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"history_evidence\",\"summary_revision_contracts\":{\"reviewing_experiences\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_82f3a412b3de683fc6fbc596\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s3\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\"]},\"current_attitudes\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_0ded4016ea43e4c8d35f4fa3\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"]},\"music_preferences\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_6a88725b5da0855a58b876cc\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"]},\"changes_in_expression\":{\"previous_version\":1,\"eligible_route_ids\":[\"fact_0578095f03f34ed22c798ec3\"],\"required_source_ids\":[\"s32\",\"s8\",\"s22\",\"s34\",\"s23\",\"s45\",\"s44\",\"s36\",\"s24\",\"s3\",\"s35\",\"s9\",\"s7\",\"s21\",\"s20\",\"s4\",\"s33\"]}},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:635511585cb4f4a0da9295a503b64ee539c38b03c02f160ace3a72e6206336de\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":168.0,\"observed_end\":168.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:41d476509de0d4e7b767eebe20704f0db44d39ab56faa7ec8081d0bfc22ccce8\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":29.0,\"observed_end\":31.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:bae454f4fe57dc35dda1965cc93898027809778211952df12ba1ac4564da3cc2\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":26.0,\"observed_end\":28.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d4\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:a778cffebd69d28ebcda63b5e6544932631898545b084b7906be70b3bd88e8c5\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":165.0,\"observed_end\":167.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d5\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:e7c973803319b0b032a23a834dfe4d7031c42cbaa315dba7d5243d255867dd55\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":24.0,\"observed_end\":25.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"],\"shared_history_texts\":{\"t0\":\"The user has had several negative experiences with music reviewing and related analytical approaches. They tried reviewing an album in 2019 but found it unproductive and felt forced to conform to a template that drained the fun out of music. They also started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but it became too time-consuming and felt like a chore, leading them to pause it. Additionally, their written reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made them less engaged and led to second-guessing their thoughts and emotional connection to music. The joy they once found in sharing perspectives on albums was overshadowed by fear of backlash. They concluded that their passion for music needed a more personal, less public outlet. They also lost interest in analyzing music halfway through, feeling it took away the joy, and recognized that their love for music lies in emotional connection rather than analytical components.\",\"t1\":\"The user currently feels that the joy they once found in sharing their perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash and external pressure from criticism. They realized their passion for music needs to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, and they are finally starting to embrace that. They have also found fulfillment in organizing a festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists, which has been a positive, community-oriented outlet. They have previously tried reviewing albums and podcasting but found those approaches unproductive, draining, or too time-consuming, leading them to prefer alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing music with friends.\",\"t2\":\"The user values a personal, emotional, and spontaneous connection with music over analytical or structured engagement. They prefer sharing music through informal means like playlists or discussions with friends rather than public reviews or content creation. They enjoy exploring diverse genres and discovering new music but find overwhelming volume daunting. They have organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists, finding fulfillment in community and cultural celebration through music. They have tried and abandoned reviewing albums, podcasting, and music theory analysis because these felt unproductive, burdensome, or joy-draining. They now embrace expressing their passion in a more personal, less public way.\",\"t3\":\"The user initially engaged in structured, public forms of music expression such as writing reviews, starting a podcast about music trends, and attempting analytical album reviews. Over time, they found these approaches too time-consuming, stressful, and misaligned with their natural spontaneous and emotional style. They experienced criticism, fear of backlash, and loss of joy. This led to a shift toward more personal, less public ways of connecting with music, such as sharing playlists, discussing music with friends, and organizing a community festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists. They now embrace a more personal and less public expression of their passion for music.\"},\"grounded_subquestion_parts\":[\"Synthesize the user's past reviewing experiences, current attitudes, music preferences, and changes in expression to understand their journey and current state.\\nEstablished reviewing_experiences: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t0\"},\"\\nEstablished current_attitudes: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t1\"},\"\\nEstablished music_preferences: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t2\"},\"\\nEstablished changes_in_expression: \",{\"text_ref\":\"t3\"}]}"}], "logical_call_index": 7, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 9918, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "48f4e5f9869972ed49c494fa0205a0ec5e82173ee210051531d7649369179f5f", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af2d71aa1d7ea503f5f191605ae295c5ad94a", "token_count_is_estimate": false, "token_estimator_id": "deployment_vllm_chat_v1", "tokenizer_id": null, "add_generation_prompt": true, "tokenization_scope": "adapted_plain_text_chat_default_server_template", "token_accounting_note": "Deployment input count; model weights and tokenizer hash are not independently verified", "tokenization_wire_sha256": "0ce6edd2146aa19257df502dd68cf6a77151d86c9ac3c26843ce770811d56346", "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"reviewing_experiences\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_82f3a412b3de683fc6fbc596\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has had several negative experiences with music reviewing and related analytical approaches. They tried reviewing an album in 2019 but found it unproductive and felt forced to conform to a template that drained the fun out of music. They also started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but it became too time-consuming and felt like a chore, leading them to pause it. Additionally, their written reviews were often criticized for not being objective, which made them less engaged and led to second-guessing their thoughts and emotional connection to music. The joy they once found in sharing perspectives on albums was overshadowed by fear of backlash. They concluded that their passion for music needed a more personal, less public outlet. They also lost interest in analyzing music halfway through, feeling it took away the joy, and recognized that their love for music lies in emotional connection rather than analytical components.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s8\", \"s22\", \"s45\", \"s44\", \"s3\", \"s7\", \"s21\", \"s20\", \"s4\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user explicitly describes multiple past experiences: reviews criticized for lack of objectivity (s3, s4), a 2019 album review attempt that felt unproductive and conformist (s7, s8), a 2018 podcast that became too time-consuming and chore-like (s20, s21, s22), and losing interest in analytical music dissection (s44, s45). These are all negative experiences with reviewing/analysis, leading to a shift toward more personal, less public expression.\",\n          \"summary_revision\": {\n            \"supersedes_route_ids\": [\"fact_82f3a412b3de683fc6fbc596\"],\n            \"previous_version\": 1,\n            \"reason\": \"Re-review of all original sources confirms the same historical facts; no new evidence or contradictions found.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"current_attitudes\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_0ded4016ea43e4c8d35f4fa3\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user currently feels that the joy they once found in sharing their perspective on albums was overshadowed by the fear of backlash and external pressure from criticism. They realized their passion for music needs to be expressed in a more personal, less public way, and they are finally starting to embrace that. They have also found fulfillment in organizing a festival celebrating Pacific Islander artists, which has been a positive, community-oriented outlet. They have previously tried reviewing albums and podcasting but found those approaches unproductive, draining, or too time-consuming, leading them to prefer alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing music with friends.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s32\", \"s8\", \"s22\", \"s34\", \"s23\", \"s45\", \"s44\", \"s36\", \"s24\", \"s3\", \"s35\", \"s9\", \"s7\", \"s21\", \"s20\", \"s4\", \"s33\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's own statements across multiple conversations establish a consistent current attitude: they have moved away from public music reviewing and structured content creation due to negative experiences with criticism, pressure, and loss of joy, and are now embracing more personal, less public forms of musical expression and community engagement, such as organizing a festival.\",\n          \"summary_revision\": {\n            \"supersedes_route_ids\": [\"fact_0ded4016ea43e4c8d35f4fa3\"],\n            \"previous_version\": 1,\n            \"reason\": \"Re-review of all original sources confirms the same current attitudes; no new evidence or contradictions found.\"\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"music_preferences\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_6a88725b5da0855a58b876cc\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user values a personal, emotional, and spontaneous connection with music over analytical or structured engagement. They prefer sharing music through informal means like playlists or discussions with friends rather than public reviews or content creation. They enjoy exploring diverse genres and discovering new music but find overwhelming volume daunting. They have organized a festival highlighting Pacific Islander artists, finding fulfillment in community and cultural celebration through music. They have tried and abandoned reviewing albums, podcasting, and music theory analysis because these felt unproductive, burdensome, or joy-draining. They now embrace expressing their passion in a more personal, less public way.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s32\", \"s8\", \"s22\", \"s34\", \"s23\", \"s45\", \"s44\", \"s36\", \"s24\", \"s3\", \"s35\", \"s9\", \"s7\", \"s21\", \"s20\", \"s4\", \"s33\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"current\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user explicitly states that external criticism made them less engaged and that they now prefer a more personal, less public way to express their passion (s3, s4). They tried reviewing albums in 2019 but found it unproductive and misaligned with their spontaneous, emotional style (s7, s8). They prefer alternative methods like sharing playlists or discussing music with friends (s9). They started a podcast in 2018 but f